  "id": "2",
  "content": "# Base picker in the New Terminal dialog (workspace) and one-click opens through the dialog\n\n## What to build\n\nThe server now accepts `POST /api/terminals { workspaceId, base?: string }`: it fetches `origin/<base>` and cuts the terminal's `gm-term/<id>` worktree from it, defaulting to the remote default branch. A failed fetch falls back to local `<base>` and adds `warnings: string[]` to the 201 response. It also serves `GET /api/workspaces/:id/branches[?fetch=1]` → `{ branches: string[], default: string, current?: string, fetched: boolean, error?: string, noCommit?: true }`.\n\nThis slice is the web side for **workspace** terminals:\n- **Base dropdown:** the New Terminal dialog gets a **Base** dropdown, filled instantly from local refs, then refreshed by a background fetch with a spinner.\n- **One-click opens:** `?workspace=` and `?project=[&agent=]` open the dialog prefilled instead of creating the terminal directly.\n- **Pane header:** shows `gm-term/<id> ← <baseBranch>`.\n- **Warnings:** shown as a dismissible notice.\n\nThe spec is `docs/prd/project-terminal-worktrees.md` (Decisions and Requirements → \"Web\").\n\n## Context: files to read before implementing\n\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx`:\n  - lines 236–260: `createOrThrow` / `create`;\n  - lines 330–375: the `?workspace=` and `?project=` effects to change;\n  - lines 425–435 and 565–572: where the dialog opens (`setNewAgent`, `setNewOpen(true)`);\n  - lines 686–712: `<NewTerminalDialog …>` and `onCreate`;\n  - lines 854–990: `NewTerminalDialog` itself;\n  - lines 992–996: the `NewTerminalBody` type and `PROJECT_OPTION = \"project:\"`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/TerminalPane.tsx` (lines 215–240) — the pane header `extra` with `data-testid=\"pane-branch\"`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/types.ts` (lines 73–106) — `TerminalInfo.worktree` (`{ id, path, branch }`) and `KeptWorktree`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.ts` (lines 20–50, 270–280, 455–460) — the server's `TerminalInfo.worktree` shape, which you extend with `baseBranch`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/terminals.ts` (`newWorktree`, `wtOf` ~lines 95–100) — `wtOf()` builds the `worktree` field of `TerminalInfo`; add `baseBranch` there.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx`:\n  - lines 1–60: setup with a mocked `TerminalView`;\n  - lines 100–200: `serve()` / `fetchMock` routes;\n  - lines 405–425: the close-dialog test pattern;\n  - lines 472–520: the test for the dialog opened with Ctrl Space n.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/api.ts` (or wherever `api`, `post`, `ApiError` are exported; grep `export class ApiError`).\n\n## Patterns to follow\n\n**Fetching in a component** — mirror the `loadKept` pattern in `Terminals.tsx` (~264): `api<T>(url)` in try/catch, keeping the last value on error. Track a per-request `gone` flag in effects, as in `StartRunDrawer.tsx` (~133–140):\n```ts\nlet gone = false;\napi<unknown>(\"/api/projects\").then((res) => { if (!gone) setProjects(projectList(res)); }, () => { if (!gone) setProjects([]); });\nreturn () => { gone = true; };\n```\n\n**Field markup** — reuse the dialog's existing classes:\n```tsx\n<label className=\"field\"><span className=\"field-label\">Base</span><select className=\"select\" …/>\n<span className=\"field-hint\">…</span></label>\n```\nFor the spinner, use `<span className=\"btn-spinner\" aria-hidden=\"true\" />` (already used in the Create button).\n\n**Tests** — add routes to `fetchMock` in `Terminals.test.tsx`: `/api/workspaces/<id>/branches` and `/api/workspaces/<id>/branches?fetch=1`. Use a deferred promise (like `postHooks.gate`) so the test can observe the spinner before the fetch answers.\n\n## Step-by-step tasks\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.ts` and `routes/terminals.ts`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: extend the `worktree` shape everywhere it is declared (`TerminalInfo`, `CreateTerminal`, the stored info, `toInfo` ~line 459) to `{ id: string; path: string; branch: string; baseBranch?: string }`, and set `baseBranch` in `wtOf()`.\n- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck`\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/types.ts`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `TerminalInfo.worktree?: { id: string; path: string; branch: string; baseBranch?: string }`; `TerminalInfo.warnings?: string[]` (only on the create response). Add `export interface BranchList { branches: string[]; default?: string; current?: string; fetched?: boolean; error?: string; noCommit?: boolean }`.\n\n### UPDATE `NewTerminalDialog` in `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: a new prop `defaultProject?: string` (project id). On open, the select is set to `${PROJECT_OPTION}${defaultProject}` when that project is in `projects`; otherwise use `defaultWorkspace` as today.\n- **IMPLEMENT**: when `ws` is a workspace id (not \"\" and not a project), render a **Base** field below Workspace:\n  - On open or workspace change, `GET /api/workspaces/<id>/branches` (local refs, fast). Fill `<select data-testid=\"new-terminal-base\">` with `branches`, preselect `default`, and keep a manual choice across refreshes when it still exists.\n  - In parallel, `GET /api/workspaces/<id>/branches?fetch=1`. While it runs, show `<span className=\"btn-spinner\" data-testid=\"new-terminal-base-loading\" />` next to the label. When it answers, replace the list. If `fetched === false`, show `<span className=\"field-hint\" data-testid=\"new-terminal-base-offline\">Offline: local branches</span>`.\n  - `noCommit: true` → disabled select, hint `No commits yet: not isolated` (`data-testid=\"new-terminal-base-nocommit\"`), and send no `base`.\n  - Ignore answers for a workspace that is no longer selected (a `gone` flag per effect).\n- **IMPLEMENT**: the submit body adds `base: <selected>` for a workspace when a branch is selected. **Create** stays enabled while the fetch runs.\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `NewTerminalBody` gains `base?: string`.\n- **GOTCHA**: \"Workspaces root\" (`ws === \"\"`) and project options show no Base field in this slice. A later slice adds the per-repo rows for projects.\n- **GOTCHA**: keep `data-autofocus` on the Workspace select, and keep Enter-to-submit.\n\n### UPDATE the one-click effects in `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx` (lines ~334–375)\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `?workspace=<id>` no longer calls `create`. It sets state to open the dialog with `defaultWorkspace = id` (add `const [newDefaults, setNewDefaults] = useState<{ workspace?: string; project?: string }>({})`), then removes the `workspace` param (replace).\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `?project=<id>[&agent=<a>]` does the same with `defaultProject = id` and `setNewAgent(<AgentInfo for a>)` when `a` is in `URL_AGENTS` and known in the agents list. It removes `project` and `agent`.\n- **IMPLEMENT**: after a create from the dialog, set `?focus=<new id>` as the old effects did (`setParams(… next.set(\"focus\", info.id) …, { replace: true })`). Clear `newDefaults` on cancel and on create.\n- **IMPLEMENT**: pass `defaultWorkspace={newDefaults.workspace ?? focusedWs}` and `defaultProject={newDefaults.project}` to the dialog.\n- **GOTCHA**: reopening a kept worktree (`create({ workspaceId, worktreeId })`, line ~558) must still create directly, with no dialog.\n- **GOTCHA**: keep the StrictMode-safe `handled` refs so the dialog opens once.\n\n### UPDATE create result handling in `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: when the create response has `warnings`, show them as a toast: `const toast = useToast()` (from `../ui/toast`; `ToastProvider` already wraps the page; tones are `\"ok\" | \"bad\" | \"live\"`), then `toast.show({ tone: \"bad\", text: warnings.join(\" \") })`. See `web/agentRequests.tsx` (~line 79) for a `show` call.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/TerminalPane.tsx` (line ~228)\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `pane-branch` text becomes `` `${term.worktree.branch} ← ${term.worktree.baseBranch}` `` when `baseBranch` is set, else just the branch, as today.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT** tests:\n  1. Opening the dialog on a workspace lists branches before the fetch answers, preselects `default` (`main`) even though `current` is `development`, and shows `new-terminal-base-loading`. After the fetch resolves, the list includes a new branch and the spinner is gone. Create posts `{ workspaceId, base: \"main\" }`.\n  2. A fetch answer with `fetched: false` shows \"Offline: local branches\", and Create still posts.\n  3. `noCommit: true` → disabled select plus the \"No commits yet\" hint, and no `base` in the body.\n  4. Navigating to `/terminals?workspace=<id>` opens the dialog prefilled (`new-terminal-workspace` value = id) and does **not** POST until Create is clicked.\n  5. `/terminals?project=<id>&agent=claude` opens the dialog with the project selected and the agent heading.\n  6. The pane header shows `gm-term/wabc ← main`.\n  7. Fix existing tests that relied on `?workspace=` creating immediately: they now click `new-terminal-create`.\n- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx`\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The New Terminal dialog on a workspace shows **Base**, preselected with the server's `default`, listed before the background fetch answers, with a spinner during the fetch.\n- [ ] After the fetch, the list refreshes, keeping the selection if it still exists.\n- [ ] A failed fetch shows \"Offline: local branches\", and **Create** works.\n- [ ] A workspace without commits shows a disabled dropdown and \"No commits yet: not isolated\".\n- [ ] Create posts `base` for workspaces only.\n- [ ] `/terminals?workspace=<id>` and `/terminals?project=<id>[&agent=]` open the dialog prefilled instead of creating a terminal. After Create, the URL has `?focus=<id>`.\n- [ ] **Open terminal** on a kept worktree still creates directly.\n- [ ] The pane header shows `gm-term/<id> ← <baseBranch>`.\n- [ ] Create-response `warnings` are shown to the user.\n- [ ] `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` pass.\n\n## Validation commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run typecheck && npm run lint\nnpm test -w graph-manager -- src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx\nnpm test\n```\n",
  "dependencies": [
